From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:57:50 +0200
Subject: ARM: dts: sun7i: cubietruck: run the RTC from the 32k crystal

The Cubietruck has a 32.768 kHz crystal. LOSC also clocks the AP6210
WiFi/Bluetooth module through CLK_OUT_A as its low-power clock, and
the module's Bluetooth radio does not work while LOSC runs from the
internal RC oscillator. Hand the crystal to the RTC so that it selects
it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-cubietruck.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-cubietruck.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-cubietruck.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-cubietruck.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-cubietruck.dts
@@ -308,6 +308,10 @@ &reg_usb2_vbus {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&rtc {
+	clocks = <&ext_osc32k>;
+};
+
 &spdif {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&spdif_tx_pin>;
-- 
Armbian

